---
import {CodeSnippet} from '../dmf-ui/code-block';
import catalog from '../../../contracts/catalog.json';
interface Props {slug:string;}
const {slug}=Astro.props;
const contract=catalog.components.find(c=>c.slug===slug);
if(!contract)throw Error(`Missing contract: ${slug}`);
const axes=Object.entries(contract.variants) as [string,string[]][];
const established=Object.entries(contract.states).filter(([,value])=>value.status!=='not-established').map(([state])=>state);
const unestablished=Object.entries(contract.states).filter(([,value])=>value.status==='not-established').map(([state])=>state);
---
<section id="contract" class="docs-section docs-prose" data-component-contract={slug}>
<h2>Component contract</h2><p>Contract v1 · experimental · acceptance status: <strong>partial</strong>. This inventory records the source; it does not certify every combination.</p>
<h3>Anatomy and properties</h3><p>Each part below includes its authored slots, explicit property types and inherited native types. Imported runtime options remain defined by their source declarations.</p>
{contract.parts.map(part=><details class="contract-part"><summary><code>{part.file.split('/').at(-1)}</code></summary><p>Slots: {part.slots.join(', ')||'None authored'}.</p>{part.native.length>0&&<p>Inherited native types: <code>{part.native.join(' · ')}</code></p>}{part.properties.length>0&&<div class="docs-table-scroll"><table class="docs-options"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Property</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th></tr></thead><tbody>{part.properties.map(property=><tr><th scope="row"><code>{property.name}</code></th><td><code>{property.type}</code></td><td>{property.optional?'No':'Yes in declared type'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>}<CodeSnippet code={part.declaration} language="ts" title={part.file.split('/').at(-1)} label={`${part.file.split('/').at(-1)} property declaration`} maxHeight={320}/></details>)}
<h3>Variants, sizes and defaults</h3>{axes.length>0?<ul>{axes.map(([axis,values])=><li><strong>{axis}:</strong> <code>{values.join(' | ')}</code></li>)}</ul>:<p>No local CVA variant axes are declared in this family. See the part types and core options for imported or family-specific choices.</p>}
<details class="contract-part"><summary>Authored defaults by part</summary><dl>{Object.entries(contract.defaults).map(([key,value])=><><dt><code>{key}</code></dt><dd><code>{String(value)}</code></dd></>)}</dl></details>
<h3>State evidence</h3><p><strong>Source vocabulary:</strong> {established.join(', ')}.</p><p><strong>Not established:</strong> {unestablished.join(', ')}.</p><p>Source vocabulary can occur in styles, native attributes or runtime code; it is not a supported visual prop. Not-established states need applicability review and must not be advertised as implemented. Compose async, empty and validation messages only through valid host APIs.</p>
<h3>Tokens and presets</h3><p>{contract.tokens.length?<code>{contract.tokens.join(', ')}</code>:'No direct semantic token reference extracted; inspect inherited styles and child parts.'}</p><p>Shared semantic roles support DMF, CB, HUI, QDI and portfolio scopes. Per-family brand acceptance remains partial. Shape, width, density and icons are supported only where the part declares them or through authored layout/slots.</p>
<h3>Responsive behavior and accessibility</h3><p>Preserve the part’s native semantics, label interactive content, allow text to wrap and test enlarged narrow RTL layouts. Icon-only actions require a stable accessible name. The behavior section above records family-specific authoring and keyboard notes.</p>
<h3>Coverage and limitations</h3><p>{contract.tests.sources.length} test files reference this family; references alone are not proof of complete acceptance. Imported native attributes and runtime types are not fully expanded by this inventory. Review the exported source for the complete API.</p><p><a href="/docs/component-contract/">Contract conventions and state taxonomy</a> · <a href="/docs/brand-mappings/">Brand source and mapping boundaries</a></p>
</section>
